page 1 (
    name: Faceted Search Patterns
    alias: FACETED-SEARCH-PATTERNS
    title: Faceted Search Patterns
    appearance {
        pageTemplate: @/standard
        templateOptions: #DEFAULT#
    }
    navigation {
        cursorFocus: firstItemOnPage
    }
    security {
        formAutoComplete: true
    }
    help {
        helpText:
            ```html
            <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Faceted Search Patterns is a reference catalog for developers and designers choosing how users find, filter, review, and compare records in Oracle APEX. Each example combines Faceted Search with a result component or supporting interaction.</p>
            <h3>When to use this catalog</h3>
            <p>Use the catalog to choose a search experience for a new page, compare result layouts, or understand how filtering works with lists, cards, reports, maps, calendars, timelines, summaries, and selection.</p>
            <h3>Components used on the home page</h3>
            <ul>
            <li><strong>Cards region:</strong> Displays each available pattern with its name, description, category badge, and Open example action.</li>
            <li><strong>Navigation Menu:</strong> Provides direct links to the individual pattern pages.</li>
            <li><strong>Shared Page Help dialog:</strong> Explains the selected page's pattern combination, components, interaction, and usage.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>How to explore the app</h3>
            <ol>
            <li><strong>Browse and search:</strong> Start with FS-01 - Content Row, FS-02 - Cards, and FS-03 - Search Only Classic Report to compare compact rows, visual cards, and tabular results.</li>
            <li><strong>Location and time:</strong> Explore FS-04 - Map, FS-05 - Calendar, and FS-06 - Timeline when records are best understood by location, scheduled date, or chronology.</li>
            <li><strong>Analysis and comparison:</strong> Explore FS-07 - Search Dashboard and FS-08 - Grouped Results for summaries and grouped lists.</li>
            <li>Open an example and change its search criteria. Observe how the result component responds, then open Help to understand the components used and how they work together.</li>
            <li>Choose a combination that suits your user's task and adapt its filtering, result presentation, and actions to your application data.</li>
            </ol>
            <h3>Understanding the examples</h3>
            <p>Employee and task examples use APEX sample data. Map and Calendar use generated demonstration records. The data illustrates each interaction; the reusable part is the component combination and page behavior.</p>
            <p>Most examples combine a native Faceted Search region with a native result component. Search Dashboard adds synchronized summaries. Each page's help identifies these supporting components.</p>
            ```
    }
    comments {
        comments: Landing page for the faceted-search examples. Use the native cards to compare the same employee dataset across focused APEX result components.
    }

    region pattern-index (
        name: Available Patterns
        type: cards
        source {
            location: localDatabase
            type: sqlQuery
            sqlQuery:
                ```sql
                select 1 as pattern_id,
                       'FS-01 - Content Row' as pattern_title,
                       'Core' as pattern_badge,
                       'Filter and sort' as pattern_subtitle,
                       'Scan employee rows, narrow the matches with filters, and open a profile or email action.' as pattern_description,
                       'fa fa-sort-amount-desc' as pattern_icon,
                       4 as target_page
                  from dual
                union all
                select 2,
                       'FS-02 - Cards',
                       'Core',
                       'Filter and arrange',
                       'Browse employee avatars and summaries, filter and sort the cards, and open a profile.',
                       'fa fa-layout-header-nav-left-cards',
                       5
                  from dual
                union all
                select 3,
                       'FS-03 - Search Only Classic Report',
                       'Core',
                       'Search only',
                       'Search employee name, job, or salary with one search facet and compare the matching table rows.',
                       'fa fa-table-search',
                       7
                  from dual
                union all
                select 4,
                       'FS-04 - Map',
                       'Extension',
                       'Filter by location',
                       'Faceted employee search paired with a location-aware map overview.',
                       'fa fa-map-marker',
                       9
                  from dual
                union all
                select 5,
                       'FS-05 - Calendar',
                       'Extension',
                       'Filter by date',
                       'Faceted search with date filtering beside a calendar result view.',
                       'fa fa-calendar',
                       10
                  from dual
                union all
                select 6,
                       'FS-06 - Timeline',
                       'Extension',
                       'Review tasks by month',
                       'Filter tasks by start month, assignee, and status, then open a task for more detail.',
                       'fa fa-clock-o',
                       12
                  from dual
                union all
                select 9, 'FS-07 - Search Dashboard', 'Extension', 'Explore matching employee metrics', 'See employee counts, job-role and cost-center metrics, plus cost-center and work-arrangement charts update with your filters.', 'fa fa-dashboard', 17
                  from dual
                union all
                select 10, 'FS-08 - Grouped Results', 'Extension', 'Browse employees by department', 'Filter employees and scan content rows grouped under department headings.', 'fa fa-list-alt', 20
                  from dual
                order by pattern_id
                ```
        }
        layout {
            sequence: 10
            slot: body
        }
        appearance {
            template: @/cards-container
            templateOptions: [
                u-colors
                t-CardsRegion--hideHeader js-addHiddenHeadingRoleDesc
            ]
        }
        componentAppearance {
            gridColumns: 4
        }
        card {
            primaryKeyColumn1: PATTERN_ID
        }
        title {
            column: PATTERN_TITLE
            cssClasses: u-color-44-text
        }
        subtitle {
            column: PATTERN_SUBTITLE
        }
        body {
            column: PATTERN_DESCRIPTION
            cssClasses: u-text-muted-color
        }
        iconAndBadge {
            iconSource: iconClassColumn
            iconColumn: PATTERN_ICON
            badgeColumn: PATTERN_BADGE
        }

        action open (
            label: Open example
            layout {
                position: secondary
                sequence: 10
            }
            behavior {
                type: redirectUrl
                targetUrl: f?p=&APP_ID.:&TARGET_PAGE.:&SESSION.::&DEBUG.:::
            }
            appearance {
                displayType: textWithIcon
                icon: fa-external-link
                cssClasses: [
                    t-Button--primary
                    t-Button--simple
                ]
            }
        )

    )

)

